{"type":"text","timestamp":1791728388148,"sessionID":"ses_ed4acc4e9ffe5KiH7I55i2MQOH","part":{"id":"prt_12b55528e001KgKGQUM1RImZ28","messageID":"msg_12b5542470017aCJsTaI2mu05c","sessionID":"ses_ed4acc4e9ffe5KiH7I55i2MQOH","type":"text","text":"Task list written to `docs/jobs/image_analysis-human-vs-ai-coding-style/tasks.md`.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Branch check:** I could not run `git branch --show-current` (no shell tool in this session), but `/workspace/.git` points to the worktree `image_analysis-human-vs-ai-coding-style` — the job's own worktree on its job branch, so proceeding is safe.\n\n**Job type note:** this is a documentation/analysis job. The deliverable is `docs/coding-style.md`; no source code should be modified. There is no render report in the job dir (nothing to render).\n\n**What I surveyed before decomposing** (to keep file lists concrete and honest):\n- State: `Todos.svelte.ts` (523 lines, ~25 mutation methods, filter orchestration, LocalStorage persistence, URL-param filter handling) vs `TimeTracking.svelte.ts` (171 lines, thin CRUD wrapper, `formatDuration` living in the store)\n- Services: 4 pure `Todo*Service`s with unit tests vs one `TimeTrackingGroupingService` (also tested — category/project/category CRUD logic lives in the store instead)\n- Routes/layouts: todos `+layout` is a bare `setContext` shell (all logic in the page), time-tracking `+layout` owns loading, sidebar, project-create modal, and a redirected `[id]` page\n- Components: ~30 todos components in `views/`, `props/`, `actions/` vs 11 time-tracking components (nav, widgets, entry, entry-create)\n- Observations already visible that the report should ground in references: human code with hardcoded English strings in `TodoCreate.svelte` vs AI code using `ts.get.timeTracking.*` everywhere; JSDoc contracts on AI code; duplicated `groupByDate` helper defined twice in time-tracking; i18n-typed catalogs; `keyManager`, `LoadingIndicator`, `SvelteDate` usage patterns\n\n**Tasks** (6, written to tasks.md):\n- TASK-1 / TASK-2 — full inventories of each feature's stack (read-only, low risk)\n- TASK-3 — layer-by-layer comparison and the both-directions style-difference list (medium: must cite file/line refs)\n- TASK-4 — cross-check against the repo's own `docs/*.md` conventions to separate human-vs-AI from idiomatic-vs-deviating (low)\n- TASK-5 — write `docs/coding-style.md` (medium: it is the entire deliverable)\n- TASK-6 — verification pass: all referenced paths/line ranges exist, no source/i18n/test file changed, plus `npm run check` (low)\n\nI did not commit anything (read-only analyst).","time":{"start":1791728374414,"end":1791728388140}}}
