{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791728516789,"sessionID":"ses_ed4aa686fffeRBfsdkp4XPbH5d","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_rOHNvLRtNSGNM0Bmwu8D9772","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && ls docs/jobs/archive/joke_time-tracking-improvements/ && echo \"=== brief head ===\" && head -40 docs/jobs/archive/joke_time-tracking-improvements/brief.md"},"output":"brief.md\nimplementation.md\nsession.log\ntasks.md\ntokens.json\nverdict.md\n=== brief head ===\n# Brief: time tracking improvements\n\ntype: feature\nid: joke\nbranch: feature/joke_time-tracking-improvements\ndate: 2026-10-10\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nRework time tracking so its UI stops hiding, duplicating, and contradicting the\ndata model it already has. The domain model is sound (projects own many\ncategories; a single running timer derived from entries), and the store/contract\nlayer plus `ActiveTimer` are solid — keep them. This job addresses the full set\nof findings in `docs/tt-assessment.md` (its §6 table is the line-level\nauthority): navigation and information architecture, the create/edit flows,\ndashboard and statistics composition, and visual/accessibility/i18n consistency.\nThe assessment changed no source; this is the follow-up implementation.\n\nNotable changes, grouped as workstreams:\n\n- **URL-driven navigation.** Move the Dashboard/Entries view (and ideally the\n  selected project) into the route or a search param so reload, deep-linking, and\n  back/forward restore the view; derive the active tab from the URL instead of\n  store state. Replace the sidebar's inline `display` toggle with the app's\n  `open`-state + transition drawer pattern used by todos/notes.\n- **Discoverable management.** Stop hiding project/category actions behind hover\n  and double-click; give icon-only buttons accessible names and make the same\n  actions reachable by touch and keyboard.\n- **Single source of truth for durations and colours.** Consume\n  `project.total_duration` and/or the statistics endpoint instead of recomputing\n  totals by hand; remove the duplicated `groupByProject` (including the\n  dashboard-shell widget's copy); colour each project from its own `color` field\n  (added per `api-brief.md`), never from its first category; replace the\n  `#1dbda5`/`#888`/`#9ca3af` literals with theme variables.\n- **Correct domain semantics.** Fix backdating so a duration-only entry anchors\n  to a defined time and lands on the day the user chose (never rolling into the\n  previous day); make the date field meaningful or hidden when exact times are\n  used; send `has_exact_times` on both create and update (the update field is\n  added per `api-brief.md`) and rely on the clarified anchor rule for\n","metadata":{"output":"brief.md\nimplementation.md\nsession.log\ntasks.md\ntokens.json\nverdict.md\n=== brief head ===\n# Brief: time tracking improvements\n\ntype: feature\nid: joke\nbranch: feature/joke_time-tracking-improvements\ndate: 2026-10-10\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nRework time tracking so its UI stops hiding, duplicating, and contradicting the\ndata model it already has. The domain model is sound (projects own many\ncategories; a single running timer derived from entries), and the store/contract\nlayer plus `ActiveTimer` are solid — keep them. This job addresses the full set\nof findings in `docs/tt-assessment.md` (its §6 table is the line-level\nauthority): navigation and information architecture, the create/edit flows,\ndashboard and statistics composition, and visual/accessibility/i18n consistency.\nThe assessment changed no source; this is the follow-up implementation.\n\nNotable changes, grouped as workstreams:\n\n- **URL-driven navigation.** Move the Dashboard/Entries view (and ideally the\n  selected project) into the route or a search param so reload, deep-linking, and\n  back/forward restore the view; derive the active tab from the URL instead of\n  store state. Replace the sidebar's inline `display` toggle with the app's\n  `open`-state + transition drawer pattern used by todos/notes.\n- **Discoverable management.** Stop hiding project/category actions behind hover\n  and double-click; give icon-only buttons accessible names and make the same\n  actions reachable by touch and keyboard.\n- **Single source of truth for durations and colours.** Consume\n  `project.total_duration` and/or the statistics endpoint instead of recomputing\n  totals by hand; remove the duplicated `groupByProject` (including the\n  dashboard-shell widget's copy); colour each project from its own `color` field\n  (added per `api-brief.md`), never from its first category; replace the\n  `#1dbda5`/`#888`/`#9ca3af` literals with theme variables.\n- **Correct domain semantics.** Fix backdating so a duration-only entry anchors\n  to a defined time and lands on the day the user chose (never rolling into the\n  previous day); make the date field meaningful or hidden when exact times are\n  used; send `has_exact_times` on both create and update (the update field is\n  added per `api-brief.md`) and rely on the clarified anchor rule for\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace && ls docs/jobs/archive/joke_time-tracking-improvements/ && echo \"=== brief head ===\" && head -40 docs/jobs/archive/joke_time-tracking-improvements/brief.md","time":{"start":1791728516746,"end":1791728516784}},"id":"prt_12b577dd0001BqU9Z8Q82vMCfJ","sessionID":"ses_ed4aa686fffeRBfsdkp4XPbH5d","messageID":"msg_12b57715b001enTamQBy3Z4wlg"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791728517028,"sessionID":"ses_ed4aa686fffeRBfsdkp4XPbH5d","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_FFE6BcweL5v1x6nc4zO95438","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && head -60 docs/jobs/archive/joke_time-tracking-improvements/verdict.md 2>/dev/null; echo \"=== impl head ===\"; head -50 docs/jobs/archive/joke_time-tracking-improvements/implementation.md 2>/dev/null"},"output":"# Verdict: time tracking improvements\n\nid: joke\nreviewer: deepseek-v4-flash (opencode-go)\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\nVerified on branch `feature/joke_time-tracking-improvements` against `main`\n(`git diff main...HEAD`). Cross-checked every task against the diff and the\nclaims in `implementation.md`. Verification evidence from the developer's own\nruns is recorded in `session.log`: `npm run check` = 0 errors / 0 warnings,\n`npm test` = 734/735 passing (the 1 failure is the pre-existing\n`logic-leaves.test.ts` StatisticWidget colour-class test, unrelated), and\n`eslint` on the changed TS files is clean. All source changes are committed;\nthe only uncommitted files are the harness-managed `session.log`/`tokens.json`.\n\nTASK-1: PASS\nnotes: `src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts` gains optional `color` on\n`TimeTrackingProject` + create/update project requests, optional\n`has_exact_times` on `UpdateTimeTrackingEntryRequest`, and a\n`TimeTrackingStatisticsRequest` type. `loadStatistics()` in\n`src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts:146` takes an optional `categoryIds`\narray and appends `category_ids` params. All additions optional/backward\ncompatible. Two nits: the `TimeTrackingStatisticsRequest` type is dead code\n(never used by `loadStatistics`, which takes inline params), and the exact\nfield/param names (`color`, `category_ids`) and `total_duration` unit are\nassumed from the missing `api-brief.md` — documented in implementation.md as\nrequired follow-up with the API owner.\n\nTASK-2: PASS\nnotes: `activeTab` removed from the store; derived from\n`page.url.searchParams.get('tab')` in `src/routes/time-tracking/+page.svelte:15`\nand `TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte:31`. Nav links have distinct targets\n(`/time-tracking`, `?tab=entries`, `?tab=statistics`) so reload/deep-link/\nback-forward restore the view; the project is already route-driven via\n`/time-tracking/[id]`. Active highlights keyed off `!activeProjectId && tab`.\n\nTASK-3: PASS\nnotes: `TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte` uses the app's drawer pattern — `open`\n`$state`, `{#if open}` + `transition:fly`, `HamburgerButton`/`CloseButton`, and\na shared `{#snippet sidebar()}` rendered into both the desktop column and the\nmobile drawer, matching `todos/TodoNavigationMobile.svelte`. Desktop layout\n(`hidden ... lg:flex`) preserved.\n\nTASK-4: PASS\nnotes: `src/lib/services/TimeTrackingGroupingService.ts` extracts\n`groupByProject` (own-project `color` with `FALLBACK_PROJECT_COLOR` theme-var\nfallback, `uncategorized` dropped, sorted by minutes). Both duplicated copies\nremoved (`DashboardView`, `dashboard/widgets/TimeTrackingWidget.svelte`);\n`TimeBreakdownWidget` typed from `ProjectBreakdown`. Covered by\n`tests/unit/services/TimeTrackingGroupingService.test.ts` (5 cases, incl. own-\ncolour-not-first-category, fallback, ignores project-less entries, no input\nmutation).\n\nTASK-5: PASS\nnotes: sidebar `projectDurations` reduce and project-detail `totalDuration`\nreduce replaced by `project.total_duration` (`TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte:207`,\n=== impl head ===\n# Implementation: time tracking improvements\n\nid: joke\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash (opencode-go)\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n## Summary\n\nReworked the Time Tracking feature end to end so its UI matches the domain\nmodel: URL-driven navigation, discoverable/accessible management, one source of\ntruth for durations and colours, a single unified entry component with correct\nbackdating, editing everywhere entries are shown, a separated statistics\nsurface, confirmed destructive actions, shared form controls, and cleaner\ni18n/heading conventions. The store/contract layer and `ActiveTimer` were kept\nas-is (only additive contract-mirror changes).\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: Updated the contract mirror in `src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts` — added\noptional `color` to `TimeTrackingProject` and to the create/update project\nrequests, added optional `has_exact_times` to `UpdateTimeTrackingEntryRequest`,\nand added a `TimeTrackingStatisticsRequest` type. `loadStatistics` in\n`src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts` now takes an optional `categoryIds` array\nand appends it as the statistics category filter.\n\nTASK-2: Made the view URL-driven. Removed `activeTab` from the store; the active\ntab is derived from `?tab=` in both `src/routes/time-tracking/+page.svelte` and\n`TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte`, and the nav links now have distinct targets\n(`/time-tracking` vs `?tab=entries`), so reload/deep-link/back-forward work.\n\nTASK-3: Replaced the sidebar's inline `style.display` toggle with the app's\n`open` `$state` + `{#if open}` + `transition:fly` drawer pattern (a shared\n`{#snippet sidebar()}` renders into both the desktop column and the mobile\ndrawer), matching todos/notes.\n\nTASK-4: Added `src/lib/services/TimeTrackingGroupingService.ts` (pure,\nunit-tested) that groups entries by project using the project's own `color`\n(theme-variable fallback), drops the impossible `uncategorized` state, and sorts\nby minutes. Replaced both `groupByProject` copies (`DashboardView`,\n`dashboard/widgets/TimeTrackingWidget`) and typed `TimeBreakdownWidget` from the\nservice. New test: `tests/unit/services/TimeTrackingGroupingService.test.ts`.\n\nTASK-5: Replaced the sidebar and project-detail duration reduces with\n`project.total_duration`.\n\nTASK-6/7/8 (landed together; same file): Unified `EntryCreate`/`EntryEdit` into\none `EntryCreate.svelte` with an optional `entry` prop and deleted\n`EntryEdit.svelte`. Both paths send consistent ISO timestamps and\n`has_exact_times` on create *and* update. Duration-only entries anchor to local\nnoon of the chosen day (never rolling into the previous day); the date field is\n","metadata":{"output":"# Verdict: time tracking improvements\n\nid: joke\nreviewer: deepseek-v4-flash (opencode-go)\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\nVerified on branch `feature/joke_time-tracking-improvements` against `main`\n(`git diff main...HEAD`). Cross-checked every task against the diff and the\nclaims in `implementation.md`. Verification evidence from the developer's own\nruns is recorded in `session.log`: `npm run check` = 0 errors / 0 warnings,\n`npm test` = 734/735 passing (the 1 failure is the pre-existing\n`logic-leaves.test.ts` StatisticWidget colour-class test, unrelated), and\n`eslint` on the changed TS files is clean. All source changes are committed;\nthe only uncommitted files are the harness-managed `session.log`/`tokens.json`.\n\nTASK-1: PASS\nnotes: `src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts` gains optional `color` on\n`TimeTrackingProject` + create/update project requests, optional\n`has_exact_times` on `UpdateTimeTrackingEntryRequest`, and a\n`TimeTrackingStatisticsRequest` type. `loadStatistics()` in\n`src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts:146` takes an optional `categoryIds`\narray and appends `category_ids` params. All additions optional/backward\ncompatible. Two nits: the `TimeTrackingStatisticsRequest` type is dead code\n(never used by `loadStatistics`, which takes inline params), and the exact\nfield/param names (`color`, `category_ids`) and `total_duration` unit are\nassumed from the missing `api-brief.md` — documented in implementation.md as\nrequired follow-up with the API owner.\n\nTASK-2: PASS\nnotes: `activeTab` removed from the store; derived from\n`page.url.searchParams.get('tab')` in `src/routes/time-tracking/+page.svelte:15`\nand `TimeTrackin