{"type":"text","timestamp":1791728901146,"sessionID":"ses_ed4a56c6fffevAGmwB1j5o7wcj","part":{"id":"prt_12b5d54bc001lGMeNNp6QQ1K5a","messageID":"msg_12b5d4bc7001ZFR7fjrERGuTDI","sessionID":"ses_ed4a56c6fffevAGmwB1j5o7wcj","type":"text","text":"Verdict written and committed on branch `feature/image_analysis-human-vs-ai-coding-style` (commit `8dc854e`).\n\n## Summary\n\n**Overall: NEEDS WORK** — the deliverable (`docs/coding-style.md`, 574 lines) is a thorough, well-evidenced human-vs-AI comparison, and the diff is cleanly scoped (report + job artifacts only; no `src/**`, `tests/**`, or i18n change). I verified the vast majority of its claims against source, tests, the five policy docs, and git history, including the sophisticated `git log -S` claim about the two stale `Todos` comments (introduced `d7d4d92`, removed `a34275e`).\n\nThree verifiable inaccuracies block merge — all in the report:\n\n1. **Wrong component count.** The report says the todos feature has **35** component files (§1 table, §4) and **15** `props/` components; the actual tree has **34** `.svelte` files and **14** under `props/`.\n2. **Wrong call-site citation** in §5: `weekBreakdown()` is at `DashboardView.svelte:63`, not `:58` (`:58` is `todayBreakdown()`).\n3. **Policy misquote** in §11: `docs/TESTING.md` does not name `TimeTrackingGroupingService` as covered pure logic.\n\nPer-task: TASK-1 PARTIAL, TASK-2/3/4/6 PASS, TASK-5 PARTIAL. `npm run check` was skipped with a valid reason (no `node_modules`, and a doc-only change can't alter type-check state).\n\nNote: the working tree still has harness-driven modifications to `AGENTS.md`, `session.log`, and `tokens.json` — I left those unstaged and committed only `verdict.md`.","time":{"start":1791728899260,"end":1791728901141}}}
