{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791728953717,"sessionID":"ses_ed4a27f91ffeR9dOCXcA8pH3kp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_ObUnbWZRF9rLras0sKL74521","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"=== report §11 exact ===\"; awk 'NR>=401 && NR<=438 {printf \"%d: %s\\n\", NR, $0}' docs/coding-style.md"},"output":"=== report §11 exact ===\n401: ## 11. Tests\n402: \n403: `docs/TESTING.md` names `Todos` as the Priority-1 store (highest logic density)\n404: and both `TodoFilterService` and `TimeTrackingGroupingService` as covered pure\n405: logic.\n406: \n407: - **Human (`todos`)** invests heavily in tests:\n408:   - Store: `tests/unit/stores/Todos.test.ts` — **367 lines**, covering\n409:     `useFilters` (backlog, hide-it, category/tag, auto-generated visibility),\n410:     URL filters, `quickCreate` recurrence-ignore, sort-by-score, hide-it\n411:     persistence/restore, and concurrency (\"respects a toggle issued while `load()`\n412:     is in flight\", `:330-365`).\n413:   - Services: `TodoFilterService.test.ts` (280), `TodoSortingService.test.ts`\n414:     (116), `TodoRelevanceService.test.ts` (96), `TodoGroupingService.test.ts` (48)\n415:     — ~540 lines.\n416:   - Components: `todos/Counter` is tested twice\n417:     (`tests/components/counter.test.ts`, `context-harness.test.ts`) and `NoTodos`\n418:     via `logic-leaves.test.ts`.\n419:   - The tests carry **explanatory \"why\" comments** — e.g. the regression note at\n420:     `Todos.test.ts:111-115` explaining a stale-filter bug. This is the human\n421:     comment style relocated into the test suite, where it is arguably most\n422:     valuable.\n423: - **AI (`time-tracking`)** tests the extracted service well but the feature\n424:   thinly:\n425:   - `tests/unit/services/TimeTrackingGroupingService.test.ts` — 96 lines, 5\n426:     cases including \"own colour, not first category\", fallback colour, ignores\n427:     project-less entries and no input mutation. Good coverage of the service.\n428:   - `tests/unit/stores/TimeTracking.test.ts` — only 64 lines: `load()`,\n429:     no-active-timer, one `startTimer`, and `formatDuration` cases. The store's\n430:     other mutators are untested (defensible — `docs/TESTING.md` §8 says not to\n431:     test boilerplate CRUD — but `loadStatistics` param building, which *is*\n432:     non-trivial, has no test).\n433:   - **No component tests** for any time-tracking widget, despite\n434:     `TimeBreakdownWidget` being a clean props-driven leaf (the exact shape\n435:     `docs/TESTING.md` §8 Priority-2 says to test).\n436: \n437: Test : source ratio is roughly **0.24 (human) vs. 0.075 (AI)**.\n438: \n","metadata":{"output":"=== report §11 exact ===\n401: ## 11. Tests\n402: \n403: `docs/TESTING.md` names `Todos` as the Priority-1 store (highest logic density)\n404: and both `TodoFilterService` and `TimeTrackingGroupingService` as covered pure\n405: logic.\n406: \n407: - **Human (`todos`)** invests heavily in tests:\n408:   - Store: `tests/unit/stores/Todos.test.ts` — **367 lines**, covering\n409:     `useFilters` (backlog, hide-it, category/tag, auto-generated visibility),\n410:     URL filters, `quickCreate` recurrence-ignore, sort-by-score, hide-it\n411:     persistence/restore, and concurrency (\"respects a toggle issued while `load()`\n412:     is in flight\", `:330-365`).\n413:   - Services: `TodoFilterService.test.ts` (280), `TodoSortingService.test.ts`\n414:     (116), `TodoRelevanceService.test.ts` (96), `TodoGroupingService.test.ts` (48)\n415:     — ~540 lines.\n416:   - Components: `todos/Counter` is tested twice\n417:     (`tests/components/counter.test.ts`, `context-harness.test.ts`) and `NoTodos`\n418:     via `logic-leaves.test.ts`.\n419:   - The tests carry **explanatory \"why\" comments** — e.g. the regression note at\n420:     `Todos.test.ts:111-115` explaining a stale-filter bug. This is the human\n421:     comment style relocated into the test suite, where it is arguably most\n422:     valuable.\n423: - **AI (`time-tracking`)** tests the extracted service well but the feature\n424:   thinly:\n425:   - `tests/unit/services/TimeTrackingGroupingService.test.ts` — 96 lines, 5\n426:     cases including \"own colour, not first category\", fallback colour, ignores\n427:     project-less entries and no input mutation. Good coverage of the service.\n428:   - `tests/unit/stores/TimeTracking.test.ts` — only 64 lines: `load()`,\n429:     no-active-timer, one `startTimer`, and `formatDuration` cases. The store's\n430:     other mutators are untested (defensible — `docs/TESTING.md` §8 says not to\n431:     test boilerplate CRUD — but `loadStatistics` param building, which *is*\n432:     non-trivial, has no test).\n433:   - **No component tests** for any time-tracking widget, despite\n434:     `TimeBreakdownWidget` being a clean props-driven leaf (the exact shape\n435:     `docs/TESTING.md` §8 Priority-2 says to test).\n436: \n437: Test : source ratio is roughly **0.24 (human) vs. 0.075 (AI)**.\n438: \n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"echo \"=== report §11 exact ===\"; awk 'NR>=401 && NR<=438 {printf \"%d: %s\\n\", NR, $0}' docs/coding-style.md","time":{"start":1791728953680,"end":1791728953711}},"id":"prt_12b5e2881001sO9rUlHnCuQywP","sessionID":"ses_ed4a27f91ffeR9dOCXcA8pH3kp","messageID":"msg_12b5e1c62001U1ZK1BJsYR5Vwi"}}
