{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791729089826,"sessionID":"ses_ed49ff389ffeIt68XBPiOrs69A","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_E6zhPlWISg4zAz0it92z0788","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/image_analysis-human-vs-ai-coding-style/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/image_analysis-human-vs-ai-coding-style/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: analysis: human vs ai coding style\n2: \n3: id: image\n4: analyst:\n5: date: 2026-10-11\n6: \n7: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n8: \n9: ## Task breakdown\n10: \n11: This is a documentation/analysis job: the deliverable is a single report file\n12: `docs/coding-style.md` comparing the human-built todos feature against the\n13: AI-built time-tracking feature. No source code may be modified. The two\n14: feature stacks are the \"read-only inputs\" listed under each task; the only\n15: file that may be created/changed is the report.\n16: \n17: Ground truth for the comparison is the repo's own conventions in\n18: `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`, `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`, `docs/COMPONENTS.md`,\n19: `docs/DATA_LAYER.md`, `docs/TESTING.md` — they were written for this\n20: codebase and both features should be measured against them, not against\n21: generic taste. Objectively verifiable metrics (file/line references, LOC,\n22: component/test counts) are essential so every \"human does X / AI does Y\"\n23: claim is checkable.\n24: \n25: TASK-1: Inventory the human-built todos feature end to end (state store, 4 pure services, types, routes, views, nav, props, actions) and collect stylistic observations with concrete file/line references.\n26:      files (read-only): src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts, src/lib/services/Todo{Services}/*.ts, src/lib/types/todo.ts, src/routes/todos/{+layout,+page}.svelte, src/lib/components/todos/** (views/, props/, actions/, TodoNavigation*, ListEntry, ScoreBar, Counter, NoTodos, ViewSwitcher)\n27:      depends: none\n28:      risk: low — pure reading; only risk is incompleteness, mitigated by enumerating the full component list.\n29: \n30: TASK-2: Inventory the AI-built time-tracking feature end to end (state store, grouping service, types, layout/pages incl. [id], nav, widgets, entry components) and collect stylistic observations with concrete file/line references.\n31:      files (read-only): src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts, src/lib/services/TimeTrackingGroupingService.ts, src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts, src/routes/time-tracking/{+layout,+page,[id]/+page}.svelte, src/lib/components/time-tracking/**\n32:      depends: none\n33:      risk: low — pure reading; same completeness caveat as TASK-1.\n34: \n35: TASK-3: Compare both features layer by layer (state service shape, layout vs page responsibilities, view/component decomposition, service extraction, types, reactivity patterns, error handling, comments, helpers reuse, i18n usage, tests) and derive the concrete style-difference list — what the human does that the AI doesn't, and vice versa.\n36:      files: none written in this task; findings feed TASK-5 (docs/coding-style.md)\n37:      depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n38:      risk: medium — subjective claims need to be grounded in file/line refs and objective metrics (counts, LOC) to be credible and avoid rework.\n39: \n40: TASK-4: Cross-check both codebases against the repo's documented conventions (docs/BEST_PRACTICES, STATE_SERVICES, COMPONENTS, DATA_LAYER, TESTING) and classify each observation as \"matches repo idiom\" vs \"deviates\", separating human-vs-AI differences from idiomatic-vs-non-idiomatic ones (note: the docs themselves are human-authored, so human deviations from them are noteworthy too).\n41:      files (read-only): docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md, docs/STATE_SERVICES.md, docs/COMPONENTS.md, docs/DATA_LAYER.md, docs/TESTING.md\n42:      depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n43:      risk: low — no code touched; risk is misquoting the policy docs, mitigated by quoting section headers/paraphrasing carefully.\n44: \n45: TASK-5: Write the full report to docs/coding-style.md — methodology, per-layer comparison, a style-characteristics table, \"what the human does that the AI doesn't\" and the reverse, concrete examples with file/line references, notes on test coverage (tests/unit/stores/{Todos,TimeTracking}.test.ts, tests/unit/services/*), and a summary of how the styles differ.\n46:      files: docs/coding-style.md (new file, the only file created; must not modify any src/** or tests/** file)\n47:      depends: TASK-3, TASK-4\n48:      risk: medium — the report is the whole deliverable; length and quality determine whether review passes, so keep claims verifiable and reference real file paths.\n49: \n50: TASK-6: Verify the report — re-read docs/coding-style.md, confirm every referenced file path and line range exists, confirm no source/test/i18n file was changed (report is purely additive), and run `npm run check` as a sanity pass to show the repo still type-checks.\n51:      files: docs/coding-style.md\n52:      depends: TASK-5\n53:      risk: low — no code changes expected; catches stale references and accidental modifications.\n\n(End of file - total 53 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: analysis: human vs ai coding style\n\nid: image\nanalyst:\ndate: 2026-10-11\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nThis is a documentation/analysis job: the deliverable is a single report file\n`docs/coding-style.md` comparing the human-built todos feature against the\nAI-built time-tracking feature. No source code may be modified. The two\nfeature stacks are the \"read-only inputs\" listed under each task; the only\nfile that may be created/changed is the report.\n\nGround truth for the comparison is the repo's own conventions in\n`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`, `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`, `docs/COMPONENTS.md`,\n`docs/DATA_LAYER.md`, `docs/TESTING.md` — they were written for this\ncodebase and both features should be measured against them, not against","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/image_analysis-human-vs-ai-coding-style/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: analysis: human vs ai coding style\n\nid: image\nanalyst:\ndate: 2026-10-11\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nThis is a documentation/analysis job: the deliverable is a single report file\n`docs/coding-style.md` comparing the human-built todos feature against the\nAI-built time-tracking feature. No source code may be modified. The two\nfeature stacks are the \"read-only inputs\" listed under each task; the only\nfile that may be created/changed is the report.\n\nGround truth for the comparison is the repo's own conventions in\n`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`, `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`, `docs/COMPONENTS.md`,\n`docs/DATA_LAYER.md`, `docs/TESTING.md` — they were written for this\ncodebase and both features should be measured against them, not against\ngeneric taste. Objectively verifiable metrics (file/line references, LOC,\ncomponent/test counts) are essential so every \"human does X / AI does Y\"\nclaim is checkable.\n\nTASK-1: Inventory the human-built todos feature end to end (state store, 4 pure services, types, routes, views, nav, props, actions) and collect stylistic observations with concrete file/line references.\n     files (read-only): src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts, src/lib/services/Todo{Services}/*.ts, src/lib/types/todo.ts, src/routes/todos/{+layout,+page}.svelte, src/lib/components/todos/** (views/, props/, actions/, TodoNavigation*, ListEntry, ScoreBar, Counter, NoTodos, ViewSwitcher)\n     depends: none\n     risk: low — pure reading; only risk is incompleteness, mitigated by enumerating the full component list.\n\nTASK-2: Inventory the AI-built time-tracking feature end to end (state store, grouping service, types, layout/pages incl. [id], nav, widgets, entry components) and collect stylistic observations with concrete file/line references.\n     files (read-only): src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts, src/lib/services/TimeTrackingGroupingService.ts, src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts, src/routes/time-tracking/{+layout,+page,[id]/+page}.svelte, src/lib/components/time-tracking/**\n     depends: none\n     risk: low — pure reading; same completeness caveat as TASK-1.\n\nTASK-3: Compare both features layer by layer (state service shape, layout vs page responsibilities, view/component decomposition, service extraction, types, reactivity patterns, error handling, comments, helpers reuse, i18n usage, tests) and derive the concrete style-difference list — what the human does that the AI doesn't, and vice versa.\n     files: none written in this task; findings feed TASK-5 (docs/coding-style.md)\n     depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n     risk: medium — subjective claims need to be grounded in file/line refs and objective metrics (counts, LOC) to be credible and avoid rework.\n\nTASK-4: Cross-check both codebases against the repo's documented conventions (docs/BEST_PRACTICES, STATE_SERVICES, COMPONENTS, DATA_LAYER, TESTING) and classify each observation as \"matches repo idiom\" vs \"deviates\", separating human-vs-AI differences from idiomatic-vs-non-idiomatic ones (note: the docs themselves are human-authored, so human deviations from them are noteworthy too).\n     files (read-only): docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md, docs/STATE_SERVICES.md, docs/COMPONENTS.md, docs/DATA_LAYER.md, docs/TESTING.md\n     depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n     risk: low — no code touched; risk is misquoting the policy docs, mitigated by quoting section headers/paraphrasing carefully.\n\nTASK-5: Write the full report to docs/coding-style.md — methodology, per-layer comparison, a style-characteristics table, \"what the human does that the AI doesn't\" and the reverse, concrete examples with file/line references, notes on test coverage (tests/unit/stores/{Todos,TimeTracking}.test.ts, tests/unit/services/*), and a summary of how the styles differ.\n     files: docs/coding-style.md (new file, the only file created; must not modify any src/** or tests/** file)\n     depends: TASK-3, TASK-4\n     risk: medium — the report is the whole deliverable; length and quality determine whether review passes, so keep claims verifiable and reference real file paths.\n\nTASK-6: Verify the report — re-read docs/coding-style.md, confirm every referenced file path and line range exists, confirm no source/test/i18n file was changed (report is purely additive), and run `npm run check` as a sanity pass to show the repo still type-checks.\n     files: docs/coding-style.md\n     depends: TASK-5\n     risk: low — no code changes expected; catches stale references and accidental modifications.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":53,"totalLines":53,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/image_analysis-human-vs-ai-coding-style/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791729089732,"end":1791729089773}},"id":"prt_12b603bb50011RvxzxCnBBEBm1","sessionID":"ses_ed49ff389ffeIt68XBPiOrs69A","messageID":"msg_12b603556001uSf6mx8fqcC42v"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791729090227,"sessionID":"ses_ed49ff389ffeIt68XBPiOrs69A","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_BzzfsykU0XTQu6Py6rR11700","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/image_analysis-human-vs-ai-coding-style/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/image_analysis-human-vs-ai-coding-style/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Implementation: analysis: human vs ai coding style\n2: \n3: id: image\n4: developer: deepseek-v4-flash (opencode-go)\n5: date: 2026-10-11\n6: \n7: ## Summary\n8: \n9: Documentation/analysis job. Produced a single read-only report,\n10: `docs/coding-style.md`, comparing the human-built `todos` feature against the\n11: AI-built `time-tracking` feature. No source, test, or i18n file was changed.\n12: \n13: ## Changes\n14: \n15: - **TASK-1 (inventory todos):** read `src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts`, the four\n16:   `src/lib/services/Todo*Service.ts`, `src/lib/types/todo.ts`, both\n17:   `src/routes/todos/**` files, all 34 `src/lib/components/todos/**` files and the\n18:   todos tests; collected line/file counts and line-level observations.\n19: - **TASK-2 (inventory time-tracking):** read `src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts`,\n20:   `src/lib/services/TimeTrackingGroupingService.ts`, `src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts`,\n21:   all three `src/routes/time-tracking/**` files, all 11\n22:   `src/lib/components/time-tracking/**` files and the time-tracking tests.\n23: - **TASK-3/4 (compare + policy cross-check):** compared both stacks layer by\n24:   layer and measured each observation against `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`,\n25:   `STATE_SERVICES.md`, `COMPONENTS.md`, `DATA_LAYER.md` and `TESTING.md`,\n26:   classifying each as \"matches repo idiom\" vs \"deviates\".\n27: - **TASK-5:** wrote `docs/coding-style.md` — methodology, metrics snapshot,\n28:   per-layer comparison, a convention-by-convention table, \"what the human does\n29:   that the AI doesn't\" and the reverse, deviations for each author, a test\n30:   coverage comparison, and a summary. Every claim is anchored to a real\n31:   file/line or a reproducible count.\n32: - **TASK-6 (verification):** re-read the report; confirmed every referenced\n33:   path exists and every cited line range is within the file; confirmed\n34:   `git status` shows no `src/**`, `tests/**` or i18n changes (report is purely\n35:   additive). `npm run check` could **not** be run because the workspace has no\n36:   `node_modules` and installing dependencies unattended is disallowed by the\n37:   project's hard rules — see Known issues.\n38: \n39: ## Post-review fixes\n40: \n41: The reviewer returned **NEEDS WORK** with three verifiable errors in\n42: `docs/coding-style.md` (`verdict.md`); all are now fixed:\n43: \n44: - **Component counts.** Corrected `35` → `34` component files in the §1 metrics\n45:   table and §4, `15` → `14` `props/` components in §4, and `35` → `34` in the §8\n46:   todos-components sentence. Re-verified with\n47:   `find src/lib/components/todos -name '*.svelte' | wc -l` = 34\n48:   (8 top-level + 14 `props/` + 8 `views/` + 4 `actions/`). The component LOC\n49:   total (2848) was already correct, and the feature totals (3849 / 2132) and\n50:   every other row of the metrics table were re-checked with `wc -l` and remain\n51:   accurate.\n52: - **§5 call-site citation.** `weekBreakdown()`/`todayBreakdown()` are invoked at\n53:   `DashboardView.svelte:63`/`:58` respectively; the text now reads\n54:   \"`todayBreakdown()`/`weekBreakdown()` (`:58,63`)\" instead of labelling both\n55:   call sites as `weekBreakdown()`.\n56: - **§11 `TESTING.md` misquote.** `docs/TESTING.md` does not name\n57:   `TimeTrackingGroupingService` as covered pure logic; the sentence now lists the\n58:   services it actually names (`TodoGroupingService`, `TodoRelevanceService`,\n59:   `TodoFilterService`).\n60: \n61: The same `35` count error in this file's TASK-1 entry was corrected to `34`.\n62: \n63: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n64: \n65: - `npm run check` was not executed as the TASK-6 sanity pass: `node_modules` is\n66:   absent in this workspace (`svelte-kit: not found`). Since the report changes\n67:   no source, the type-check state is unchanged. Re-run `npm ci && npm run check`\n68:   in an environment with dependencies to close the task literally.\n69: - Leftover harness/earlier-agent files were committed to leave the worktree\n70:   clean: `docs/jobs/image_analysis-human-vs-ai-coding-style/session.log`\n71:   (grew during the analyst session), `tokens.json` (analyst token record), and\n72:   the root `AGENTS.md` (synced to the committed `docs/AGENTS.md`, which already\n73:   carried the added \"Coding policies\" section; the root copy was stale).\n74: - The report notes that the policy doc `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` quotes two\n75:   \"why\" comments from `Todos.svelte.ts` that no longer exist (they were removed\n76:   in commit `a34275e`). That is a doc-vs-code drift that may be worth fixing\n77:   separately — out of scope here.\n\n(End of file - total 77 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation: analysis: human vs ai coding style\n\nid: image\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash (opencode-go)\ndate: 2026-10-11\n\n## Summary\n\nDocumentation/analysis job. Produced a single read-only report,\n`docs/coding-style.md`, comparing the human-built `todos` feature against the\nAI-built `time-tracking` feature. No source, test, or i18n file was changed.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **TASK-1 (inventory todos):** read `src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts`, the four\n  `src/lib/services/Todo*Service.ts`, `src/lib/types/todo.ts`, both\n  `src/routes/todos/**` files, all 34 `src/lib/components/todos/**` files and the\n  todos tests; collected line/file counts and line-level observations.\n- **TASK-2 (inventory time-tracking):** read `src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts`,\n  `src/lib/services/TimeTrackingGroupingService.ts`, `src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts`,","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/image_analysis-human-vs-ai-coding-style/implementation.md","text":"# Implementation: analysis: human vs ai coding style\n\nid: image\ndeveloper: deepseek-v4-flash (opencode-go)\ndate: 2026-10-11\n\n## Summary\n\nDocumentation/analysis job. Produced a single read-only report,\n`docs/coding-style.md`, comparing the human-built `todos` feature against the\nAI-built `time-tracking` feature. No source, test, or i18n file was changed.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **TASK-1 (inventory todos):** read `src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts`, the four\n  `src/lib/services/Todo*Service.ts`, `src/lib/types/todo.ts`, both\n  `src/routes/todos/**` files, all 34 `src/lib/components/todos/**` files and the\n  todos tests; collected line/file counts and line-level observations.\n- **TASK-2 (inventory time-tracking):** read `src/lib/state/TimeTracking.svelte.ts`,\n  `src/lib/services/TimeTrackingGroupingService.ts`, `src/lib/types/time_tracking.ts`,\n  all three `src/routes/time-tracking/**` files, all 11\n  `src/lib/components/time-tracking/**` files and the time-tracking tests.\n- **TASK-3/4 (compare + policy cross-check):** compared both stacks layer by\n  layer and measured each observation against `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`,\n  `STATE_SERVICES.md`, `COMPONENTS.md`, `DATA_LAYER.md` and `TESTING.md`,\n  classifying each as \"matches repo idiom\" vs \"deviates\".\n- **TASK-5:** wrote `docs/coding-style.md` — methodology, metrics snapshot,\n  per-layer comparison, a convention-by-convention table, \"what the human does\n  that the AI doesn't\" and the reverse, deviations for each author, a test\n  coverage comparison, and a summary. Every claim is anchored to a real\n  file/line or a reproducible count.\n- **TASK-6 (verification):** re-read the report; confirmed every referenced\n  path exists and every cited line range is within the file; confirmed\n  `git status` shows no `src/**`, `tests/**` or i18n changes (report is purely\n  additive). `npm run check` could **not** be run because the workspace has no\n  `node_modules` and installing dependencies unattended is disallowed by the\n  project's hard rules — see Known issues.\n\n## Post-review fixes\n\nThe reviewer returned **NEEDS WORK** with three verifiable errors in\n`docs/coding-style.md` (`verdict.md`); all are now fixed:\n\n- **Component counts.** Corrected `35` → `34` component files in the §1 metrics\n  table and §4, `15` → `14` `props/` components in §4, and `35` → `34` in the §8\n  todos-components sentence. Re-verified with\n  `find src/lib/components/todos -name '*.svelte' | wc -l` = 34\n  (8 top-level + 14 `props/` + 8 `views/` + 4 `actions/`). The component LOC\n  total (2848) was already correct, and the feature totals (3849 / 2132) and\n  every other row of the metrics table were re-checked with `wc -l` and remain\n  accurate.\n- **§5 call-site citation.** `weekBreakdown()`/`todayBreakdown()` are invoked at\n  `DashboardView.svelte:63`/`:58` respectively; the text now reads\n  \"`todayBreakdown()`/`weekBreakdown()` (`:58,63`)\" instead of labelling both\n  call sites as `weekBreakdown()`.\n- **§11 `TESTING.md` misquote.** `docs/TESTING.md` does not name\n  `TimeTrackingGroupingService` as covered pure logic; the sentence now lists the\n  services it actually names (`TodoGroupingService`, `TodoRelevanceService`,\n  `TodoFilterService`).\n\nThe same `35` count error in this file's TASK-1 entry was corrected to `34`.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- `npm run check` was not executed as the TASK-6 sanity pass: `node_modules` is\n  absent in this workspace (`svelte-kit: not found`). Since the report changes\n  no source, the type-check state is unchanged. Re-run `npm ci && npm run check`\n  in an environment with dependencies to close the task literally.\n- Leftover harness/earlier-agent files were committed to leave the worktree\n  clean: `docs/jobs/image_analysis-human-vs-ai-coding-style/session.log`\n  (grew during the analyst session), `tokens.json` (analyst token record), and\n  the root `AGENTS.md` (synced to the committed `docs/AGENTS.md`, which already\n  carried the added \"Coding policies\" section; the root copy was stale).\n- The report notes that the policy doc `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md` quotes two\n  \"why\" comments from `Todos.svelte.ts` that no longer exist (they were removed\n  in commit `a34275e`). That is a doc-vs-code drift that may be worth fixing\n  separately — out of scope here.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":77,"totalLines":77,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/image_analysis-human-vs-ai-coding-style/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791729090013,"end":1791729090210}},"id":"prt_12b603cc9001L0ErEjoiHLe101","sessionID":"ses_ed49ff389ffeIt68XBPiOrs69A","messageID":"msg_12b603556001uSf6mx8fqcC42v"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791729090241,"sessionID":"ses_ed49ff389ffeIt68XBPiOrs69A","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02_JsF7YiicdIVsc7vip4Mo2232","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/image_analysis-human-vs-ai-coding-style/verdict.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/image_analysis-human-vs-ai-coding-style/verdict.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Verdict: analysis: human vs ai coding style\n2: \n3: id: image\n4: reviewer: deepseek-v4-flash (opencode-go)\n5: date: 2026-10-11\n6: \n7: ## Review\n8: \n9: TASK-1: PARTIAL\n10: notes: Inventory is complete and every cited file/line exists — store DI at\n11: `Todos.svelte.ts:62-72`, service fields `:57-60`, `SvelteDate` filter pipeline\n12: `:165-171`, `load()` `:74-97`, `loadWorkspaces` retry `:107-118`,\n13: `quickCreate {ok,recurrenceIgnored}` `:249-278`; spinner leaks in\n14: `props/Title.svelte:59-61`, `Description.svelte:93-95`, `Subtask.svelte:66-68`,\n15: `ListAndAdd.svelte:60-62` (with `Category.svelte:70` as the correct\n16: counter-example); hardcoded strings in `Counter.svelte:8`, `KanbanView.svelte:27-40`,\n17: `Recurrence.svelte:116,125,144,150`, `TodoCreate.svelte:121,131,135,139,143,147,159`;\n18: `getBgColor` duplicated `Card.svelte:31-40` / `CompactCard.svelte:15-24`;\n19: `ScoreBar.svelte:29` commented-out fragment; `role=\"button\"` in exactly 6 files.\n20: BUT the component count is wrong: the report states **35** component files\n21: (§1 metrics table and §4) and **15** tiny components under `props/` (§4). The\n22: actual tree has **34** `.svelte` files and **14** under `props/`\n23: (`glob src/lib/components/todos/**`). Fix the counts (34 / 14) and any total\n24: derived from them.\n25: \n26: TASK-2: PASS\n27: notes: Verified end to end: store 171 LOC, field-initialiser DI `:26-31`,\n28: `load()` `:33-40`, `formatDuration` `:155-160`, hand-built query string\n29: `:146-153`; service docblock `TimeTrackingGroupingService.ts:13-17`; `groupByDate`\n30: duplicated verbatim in `GroupedEntries.svelte:18-30` and `[id]/+page.svelte:67-79`;\n31: `aria-label` at `TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte:184,212,224,245,300,308` and\n32: `ProjectCreate.svelte:102,113`; `PomodoroWidget.svelte` 211 LOC imported nowhere;\n33: dead `TimeTrackingStatisticsRequest`; no `notifications.*` anywhere.\n34: \n35: TASK-3: PASS\n36: notes: Layer-by-layer comparison is supported by the evidence (mixed return\n37: semantics `Todos.svelte.ts:280-317` vs `:331-359`; `$derived(() => …)` misuse\n38: exactly at `DashboardView.svelte:24,35,37,46` + `StatisticsView.svelte:52`;\n39: loading discipline; i18n/a11y reversal; test footprint). One minor\n40: mis-citation: §5 says `weekBreakdown()` is called at `DashboardView.svelte:58,63`\n41: — line 58 is `todayBreakdown()`, line 63 is `weekBreakdown()`. Correct the\n42: citation.\n43: \n44: TASK-4: PASS\n45: notes: Every policy quotation checks out against `docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`\n46: (comments cite `Todos`, `$derived` discipline), `STATE_SERVICES.md` (Todos as DI\n47: reference, Clipboard as \"older — not the target style\", member ordering, service\n48: delegation, `load()`+`loaded`), `COMPONENTS.md` (local UI state, loading\n49: feedback, primitives, accessibility, i18n), `DATA_LAYER.md` (layout calls\n50: `load()`, no hand-built URLs) and `TESTING.md` (Todos as Priority-1). The §8\n51: claim that `BEST_PRACTICES.md` quotes two `Todos` comments that no longer exist is\n52: true and precisely dated: `git log -S` shows both introduced in `d7d4d92` and\n53: removed in `a34275e`. Minor: §11 asserts TESTING.md names\n54: `TimeTrackingGroupingService` as covered pure logic — TESTING.md does not mention\n55: that service; reword or drop.\n56: \n57: TASK-5: PARTIAL\n58: notes: `docs/coding-style.md` (574 lines) exists, is purely additive, and is\n59: substantively accurate and well-evidenced — but it carries the component-count\n60: error from TASK-1 and the `DashboardView` line mis-cita